{"kind":"request","text":"Let a Worker create children under every register it has installed\n\nScope: from finding 72d96e46 and ruling a555fc77. admitChildCreation\nadmits a new child only when its ancestry ends at the current\nREGISTER_SCOPE. A Worker that moves to a new cohort's register\ntherefore strands every earlier room: it stays readable and stops\ncreating inboxes, lanes and other children. That blocks every cohort\nupgrade on a Worker with live rooms, hosted or self-hosted.\n\nThe scene: an operator installs a new register on a Worker that\nalready serves rooms. New rooms use the new register. Existing rooms\nkeep creating children under their own registers.\n\nThe work:\n\n1. Name the set of registers a Worker admits for child creation:\n   the current REGISTER_SCOPE for new rooms, plus each earlier\n   register that the Worker installed. Say where that set lives and\n   who changes it. A change is an operator act with a record, never\n   inferred from a request.\n2. Keep the single-register refusal for a register outside that set.\n3. Witness: a Worker with two installed registers, a room under the\n   older one creating an inbox and a lane after the switch, and a\n   control showing that an uninstalled register still refuses.\n\nDone when that scene passes on a local Worker with the controls, a\nfrozen gate passes, the checker reviews, and the head lands on main.\nWrite the design first if it needs a new record form, and say whether\nit does.\n\nOrder: after O3 lands, before any cohort deployment on a Worker with\nlive rooms.","body":{"conditions":"A Worker with two installed registers lets a room under the older one create an inbox and a lane after the switch, an uninstalled register still refuses, a frozen gate passes, the checker reviews, and the head lands on main.","target_head":"9c1556fa77d72c795e8287fef52eaf018d74730c","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c